  "question": "According to Executive Summary.pdf, how should quality risks and data/copyright risks be mitigated? Cover both.",
  "result": {
    "answer": "To mitigate quality risks where AI outputs might be inaccurate or unengaging, the documents recommend maintaining humans-in-the-loop for review, starting with conservative content generation, and gathering student feedback early [S1]. To mitigate data/copyright risks regarding the unauthorized use of licensed content, the documents recommend conducting a legal review of sources, using public or open data, ensuring model outputs are sufficiently rephrased, and citing official guidelines [S1].",
